WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.075
- All right, gov, I'm
skipping the intro today

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.745
and we're gonna max
out the time here.

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.513
This morning, President Trump

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.782
was on Hugh Hewitt's radio show

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:19.185
and Hugh asked him
about firing Fauci.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.654
And Trump's exact quote was,

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.790
"You are not allowed
to fire him."

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.426
I suspect you probably
have a different take

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:30.696
on what you can do with these
civil servants like Fauci.

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:31.931
- Sure.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.166
Well, first of all, it's
important to point out

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.035
for a long time, that
was not his excuse.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:38.004
His excuse had been
that if you fired Fauci,

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.974
both the Democrats and the
media would've pitched a fit,

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:43.676
which of course is a
hundred percent true.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.278
But that's the
price of leadership,

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.580
you gotta stand up
and do what's right.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.882
Clearly he could have been fired

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.017
from the White House task force.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.319
There was no obligation
to run him out

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.688
at press conference
after press conference,

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.490
have him doing media interviews,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.658
you know, during the height of

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.193
kind of the COVID stuff in 2020,

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:05.331
Fauci would do local hits in
Florida media, attacking me

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:08.300
for having schools open and
some of these other stuff.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.203
So there was no
obligation to do that.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.740
I think you could have
also fired him from NIH

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.477
because he had basically
committed misconduct

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.278
with the gain of function.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:23.015
You also had him saying that
it was naturally occurring

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:24.751
when they knew it
was a lab leak.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.553
All that stuff has come out now.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.621
So I think, yes, you fire him.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.523
And here's the thing, Dave,

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.392
if it's the right
thing to do, you do it.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.360
If they sue you, they sue you.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.529
But you had the basis to do that

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:37.996
and you should have done it

00:01:37.996 --> 00:01:40.834
and the country would've been
better off had he done it.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.303
- So I wanna talk a bit more
about Trump in a moment.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:46.172
But it does seem like
in the last couple days

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.308
that COVID is coming back.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.742
Somehow they're
bringing COVID back,

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.278
or they want us to
think COVID's back.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.847
Whoopi on The View
has COVID now,

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.749
Dr. Jill Biden has COVID.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:02:01.654
Florida clearly is ground
zero for protecting the people

00:02:02.454 --> 00:02:03.689
from government overreach.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.157
What would you be
doing right now

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:08.261
for the rest of the country
if you were president?

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.630
- Cleaning out
the CDC, NIH, FDA,

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:15.001
all these agencies that
failed us during COVID.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:18.404
We need a reckoning for what
they did to this country.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:21.507
And yes, in Florida, we
fought back against it.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.744
There were other states like
what Kim Reynolds did in Iowa

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.980
to make sure kids were in
school and to push back.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.849
But there are parts
of this country

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:33.520
that were really, really
harmed because of the Faucism.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.554
And yet they were
wrong about lockdowns,

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:37.389
they were wrong
about forced masking,

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:39.592
they were wrong about
school closures,

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.661
they were wrong
about mRNA vaccines

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.363
and yet nobody's been
held accountable.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:48.368
And it's my view that until
there's accountability,

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.069
they're gonna keep
trying it again.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:53.106
I mean, the notion that
you have a school district

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:56.209
in the DC suburbs, I
think Montgomery County

00:02:56.209 --> 00:03:00.513
imposing masks in 2023 shows

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.714
that you give these
people an inch,

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.982
they're gonna take a mile.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.118
So we need that accountability.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.119
We are gonna bring reckoning,

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.756
we are gonna turn those
agencies inside and out.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.190
We need people.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.592
We don't need Faucis running
around those agencies.

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:15.828
We need people like my
surgeon general in Florida,

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:20.032
Dr. Joseph Ladapo, who was
right against the lockdowns.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:23.335
He was right against the
force masking from day one.

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:24.803
That's what we need.

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:27.640
We need people like Dr.
Bhattacharya from Stanford.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.875
So, I think they're
gonna keep trying this.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.878
In Florida, we've enacted
permanent protection.

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:35.848
So you can't force
anybody to wear a mask.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.517
You can't force kids
to mask in school,

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.052
you can't close
businesses, none of that.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:41.854
We saw that this
would be something

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.623
that would likely
happen in the future.

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:46.626
And so we put in
permanent protections.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.394
But that should be
the order of the day

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.862
throughout this country.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.598
So, accountability
for what happened.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:53.933
And just think about it.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:56.035
Not only did you
infringe freedom,

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:58.905
not only did you lie about
things like vaccines,

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:02.942
the federal government went
additional $6 trillion in debt

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.978
over COVID with the response.

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:07.346
That's more debt
than we racked up

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:10.750
in like the first 200
years of this country.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.017
And yet people don't
want to talk about it.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:13.987
The only person that
stood up at the time

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.888
was Congressman Thomas Massey.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:18.290
And he was pilloried,
but he was right.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:22.361
So we are going to
have a reckoning when
I'm the president.

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.663
- I know you've tried
to take the high road

00:04:24.663 --> 00:04:27.333
when some of these Trump
attacks are coming your way,

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:30.269
but when he goes off on
Florida and the COVID response,

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:33.172
implies that somehow New
York did a better job

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.641
or something like that.

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:37.743
I mean, do you want
to hit him harder?

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:38.678
I understand you're
running a campaign

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.179
and you're running a state.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.114
But what do you think
the policy should be

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.549
on this sort of thing?

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.952
Because in some ways it
seems like a no-win situation

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.419
with the base to some extent.

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:49.956
- No, look, I think honestly,
I think he hurts himself.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.358
Nobody in the
Republican base thinks

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.794
New York handled COVID
better than Florida.

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:57.296
Nobody believes that.

00:04:57.296 --> 00:04:59.098
It's not believable.

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.866
And in fact, he
doesn't believe it

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:03.869
because he said for years
how good Florida did.

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:07.206
He said I was one of the
great governors in America.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.076
All of this stuff
was kind of gospel.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.944
Nobody ever questioned it

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:15.047
until about three days
before the midterm elections.

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:18.084
He saw that I was fixing
to win a landslide

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:19.652
and he started attacking me.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.186
And then that's basically be it.

00:05:21.186 --> 00:05:23.489
Just because he believes that
I'm a threat to his ambitions.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:26.058
That's the only reason
he's saying this.

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:29.161
If he didn't believe that, he
wouldn't be saying any of it.

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:30.896
So it's obviously bogus.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:34.600
I mean, half the country
visited Florida over COVID

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.970
and you're trying to
say California, New
York, and Illinois

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.038
handled it better.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.472
Give me a break.

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:43.775
So sometimes I think, you
know, you should be responding.

00:05:43.775 --> 00:05:46.578
But I think sometimes like
the more he does that,

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:48.046
I think it helps me

00:05:48.046 --> 00:05:50.249
because I kind of wish
like he had broader reach

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.784
with some of his social media.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.919
'Cause I think just putting
that stuff out there,

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:56.823
I think it hurts his
credibility more than anything,

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:59.659
especially because he's
on the record saying

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:02.361
how good a job we've done
in Florida in the past,

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:05.464
and especially because his
entire family moved to Florida

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.433
under my governorship.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.967
- Yeah.

00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:10.703
What's your message to the
ride or die Trump people,

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:13.406
like the hardcore mega base

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:15.641
that before all of
this they loved you,

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.910
but they're just
going with Trump,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.479
but you know that you have
to get some of those people

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:21.981
to win this thing.

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:26.018
- Well, nobody in the United
States in the Republican Party

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.520
has delivered more

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.723
on America First policies
and principles than me.

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.793
If you look at immigration,
illegal immigration,

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.428
we've banned sanctuary cities,

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:37.029
we've cracked down
on human smuggling,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:40.599
we even sent illegal aliens to
beautiful Martha's Vineyard.

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:43.169
And so we've put our
money where our mouth is.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:45.070
You talk about
things like China,

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.672
we've banned the
purchase of land

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:49.708
by the CCP and its
affiliates in our state.

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:52.445
We got rid of things
like Confucius Institutes

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:55.515
and we cracked down on their
influence of universities.

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:57.115
You look at what we've done for

00:06:57.115 --> 00:07:00.285
expand Second Amendment rights
with constitutional carry.

00:07:00.285 --> 00:07:03.789
Look at what we've done to
fight against the woke agenda,

00:07:03.789 --> 00:07:06.659
whether it's fighting
Disney involving education

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:08.694
or fighting this ESG movement,

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:11.464
which is really
bad for our economy

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.132
and for American families,

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:15.968
the way they're going after
domestic energy production.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.137
You wanna talk about
draining the swamp?

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:21.073
There's one guy in
this entire country

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:22.641
that's ever taken action

00:07:22.641 --> 00:07:25.945
against Soro's backed
prosecutors, and that's me.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.347
And we've removed two
of them from office

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:30.783
in the last year,
year and a half

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.785
who were not following the law

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:36.188
and were putting their political
agenda over public safety.

00:07:36.188 --> 00:07:39.825
I cleared out the election
supervisors in South Florida

00:07:39.825 --> 00:07:41.260
when I became governor.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:44.730
We've banned Zuckerbucks,
we've banned ballot harvesting,

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.132
We have universal voter ID,

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:50.469
and we even have an
election crimes task force,

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.239
police force in state government

00:07:53.239 --> 00:07:55.007
which prosecutes voter fraud.

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:57.876
So we have the best
election integrity

00:07:57.876 --> 00:07:59.311
in the entire country.

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:02.247
So I think in terms of
delivering on these things,

00:08:02.247 --> 00:08:04.649
nobody's delivered
more than I have.

00:08:04.649 --> 00:08:07.453
And everything I promised
the voters I would do,

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:10.188
I've delivered on and
exceeded those promises.

00:08:10.188 --> 00:08:12.791
And so you've got a guy
like me going in there,

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:15.227
you know, you'll have
two terms of somebody

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:18.731
that the people in Washington
do not wanna see up there,

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:21.267
the corporate press does
not wanna see me up there,

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.135
and the Democrats don't
wanna see me up there.

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:26.338
Because they realize I
don't just say this stuff

00:08:26.338 --> 00:08:27.606
in a campaign season,

00:08:27.606 --> 00:08:29.342
when I tell you I'm
gonna do something,

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:31.109
I follow through and I do it.

00:08:31.109 --> 00:08:33.412
- Is that the weird thing about
your campaign at the moment,

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:36.348
that in some ways Trump
and the mainstream media

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:38.884
are on the same side
when it comes to you

00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:41.353
and that is some seriously
strange bedfellow stuff?

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:42.588
- Yeah.

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:43.389
Well, I mean, you know,
you were in Milwaukee

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:44.323
for that debate.

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:46.392
The night before the debate,

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:48.794
Trump's main campaign operatives

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:52.164
were whining and dining
corporate journalists

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:56.035
from NBC, New York
Times, Washington Post,

00:08:56.035 --> 00:08:58.904
all these outlets that
he had always said

00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:01.607
were the enemy of
the American people

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:03.575
and yet they're colluding

00:09:03.575 --> 00:09:06.145
to basically try to
put dirt out on me.

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:08.080
And I think that
they've developed

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.717
a really unhealthy
symbiotic relationship

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:15.454
because the corporate press
wants Trump to be the nominee.

00:09:15.454 --> 00:09:17.256
Partially 'cause he's
better for ratings,

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:18.624
but partially because they think

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:20.525
that means the
Democrats will win.

00:09:20.525 --> 00:09:22.461
And they don't want
me to be the nominee

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:25.063
because they know
I will run Biden

00:09:25.063 --> 00:09:27.266
ragged around this
country, beat him.

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:28.800
But more importantly than that,

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:31.437
they know I will actually
convert on all this stuff.

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:34.073
They want to see America
continue to decline.

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:35.608
I mean, that's what they want.

00:09:35.608 --> 00:09:36.908
They don't wanna see
a guy like me come in,

00:09:36.908 --> 00:09:40.079
reverse that decline and
put us on a better path.

00:09:40.079 --> 00:09:41.614
So they're doing
everything they can

00:09:41.614 --> 00:09:43.281
to try to shape the
battlefield accordingly.

00:09:43.281 --> 00:09:48.053
But they work very closely
with some of Trump's henchmen

00:09:48.053 --> 00:09:50.956
to put out as much
dirt on me as they can.

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:53.158
Now, the stuff they
put out is ridiculous,

00:09:53.158 --> 00:09:55.194
but they do it and
they do it a lot.

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:56.929
And it just shows you,

00:09:56.929 --> 00:09:59.899
you know, who they
perceive as the threat.

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:00.900
- Is it tough for you personally

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.334
to hear some of the nonsense.

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:04.837
I mean, I feel like I've
gotten to know you fairly well

00:10:04.837 --> 00:10:07.039
and it seems like it just
kind of rolls off your back.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.841
But when you see the
really crazy stuff

00:10:08.841 --> 00:10:11.610
that he's throwing at you,
does it ever bother you

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.946
or the first lady or anything?

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:15.481
- I think we both
just understand

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:18.016
one, it goes with the territory.

00:10:18.016 --> 00:10:21.354
Two, they're shooting at you
because you're over the target.

00:10:21.354 --> 00:10:23.088
That's just the nature of it.

00:10:23.088 --> 00:10:25.257
And then three, I think
some of it's so ridiculous

00:10:25.257 --> 00:10:28.627
that I just think people
are smart enough to know

00:10:28.627 --> 00:10:29.829
that it's a bunch of bull

00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:31.764
and I think that they
just discount it.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:34.867
They understand this as
political silly season

00:10:34.867 --> 00:10:36.035
and you just do it.

00:10:36.035 --> 00:10:37.903
Now, look, I mean, I think,

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:42.875
you know, there are some folks
out there online or whatnot

00:10:44.076 --> 00:10:45.911
that kind of excuse
some of the nonsense,

00:10:45.911 --> 00:10:47.546
whereas if the shoe
were on the other foot,

00:10:47.546 --> 00:10:48.581
they'd be singing
a different tune.

00:10:48.581 --> 00:10:50.916
But that's fine, we get that.

00:10:50.916 --> 00:10:53.586
But at the end of the
day, what are we gonna do?

00:10:53.586 --> 00:10:54.987
We're not gonna
fight the good fight

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:56.555
because we're worried
about someone may

00:10:56.555 --> 00:10:58.057
say something mean about us.

00:10:58.057 --> 00:11:00.426
I mean, what I always
tell people is,

00:11:00.426 --> 00:11:03.162
in this day and age, when you're
standing for what's right,

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:04.397
it's not gonna be cost free.

00:11:04.397 --> 00:11:07.132
Our country wouldn't
be in the state it's in

00:11:07.132 --> 00:11:09.434
if doing what was
right was easy.

00:11:09.434 --> 00:11:10.936
You go out there,

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:12.571
I mean, you have moms going
to school board meetings,

00:11:12.571 --> 00:11:14.173
they're getting
attacked by the media,

00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:16.142
they're being
surveilled by the FBI.

00:11:16.142 --> 00:11:18.010
So leadership comes with a cost.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.878
There is a cost to
standing for what's right

00:11:19.878 --> 00:11:21.247
in this day and age.

00:11:21.247 --> 00:11:22.648
And the way I view it is,

00:11:22.648 --> 00:11:23.916
whatever I'm having
to do in terms of

00:11:23.916 --> 00:11:26.284
taking that type of incoming,

00:11:26.284 --> 00:11:28.487
that's not even in
the same universe

00:11:28.487 --> 00:11:31.023
as what people in
prior generations

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:33.125
have had to do to
preserve our freedom.

00:11:33.125 --> 00:11:34.492
And you can just see that,

00:11:34.492 --> 00:11:36.495
just try visiting Arlington
National Cemetery.

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:39.999
You see people that gave the
last full measure of devotion

00:11:39.999 --> 00:11:41.267
for service of the country.

00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:42.735
So you're not gonna
see me whining

00:11:42.735 --> 00:11:44.670
about somebody calling me names.

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.706
- Let's try to hit as
many big topics as we can

00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:47.973
in the time remaining.

00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:49.508
One thing that I keep
hearing from people

00:11:49.508 --> 00:11:51.777
and when I was in Milwaukee,
a few people did say it to me.

00:11:51.777 --> 00:11:56.482
They wanna hear you expand on
the Ukraine situation more.

00:11:56.482 --> 00:12:00.319
That at first sounded like you
gave that statement to Tucker

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:01.720
that felt more isolationist

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.389
then maybe you pulled
back on that a little bit.

00:12:04.389 --> 00:12:06.124
I know we have only a
certain amount of time here,

00:12:06.124 --> 00:12:07.760
but I mean, do you wanna
lay that out a bit more?

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.095
- Yeah, sure. I mean,
what they said was,

00:12:10.095 --> 00:12:11.363
I was asked after that

00:12:11.363 --> 00:12:13.265
whether I thought
Putin was a good guy.

00:12:13.265 --> 00:12:14.733
And I said, of course not.

00:12:14.733 --> 00:12:16.068
But that doesn't mean that

00:12:16.068 --> 00:12:18.404
we should be writing
a blank check

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:21.473
with no concept of
what our interests are

00:12:21.473 --> 00:12:23.141
or what the victory is.

00:12:23.141 --> 00:12:26.945
So we've been pretty consistent
actually on all this.

00:12:26.945 --> 00:12:30.515
We need to end this
war, no blank check,

00:12:30.515 --> 00:12:32.650
Europe needs to step up.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:35.687
And anything we do should be
in America's national interest.

00:12:35.687 --> 00:12:38.223
You don't subcontract out
your national interest

00:12:38.223 --> 00:12:39.925
to other countries.

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:41.260
And I don't think it's
been in our interest

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.829
to be sending money
to pay pensions

00:12:43.829 --> 00:12:46.565
for Ukrainian bureaucrats

00:12:46.565 --> 00:12:49.068
and salaries for
Ukrainian bureaucrats.

00:12:49.068 --> 00:12:50.569
So what I would do as president,

00:12:50.569 --> 00:12:53.973
I would use the leverage
that we have available to us

00:12:53.973 --> 00:12:55.875
to bring the conflict to an end

00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:58.844
in a way that this isn't
gonna continue to be an issue

00:12:58.844 --> 00:13:00.212
for the next 50 or 60 years.

00:13:00.212 --> 00:13:01.647
I mean, just think with Biden,

00:13:01.647 --> 00:13:04.850
his energy policy is
benefiting Russia.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:08.754
It's fueling their ability to
wage war in the first place.

00:13:08.754 --> 00:13:10.122
It's benefiting Iran,

00:13:10.122 --> 00:13:11.924
he just gave Iran 6 billion.

00:13:11.924 --> 00:13:13.592
What is Iran doing
with that money?

00:13:13.592 --> 00:13:17.329
Partially they're sending
to Russia to help Russia.

00:13:17.329 --> 00:13:20.932
China, he wants us to be
more dependent on China.

00:13:20.932 --> 00:13:22.400
They're obviously
benefiting Russia.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.237
So you can turn all of
those leverage points on,

00:13:25.237 --> 00:13:26.705
but then also use the leverage

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:28.407
that we have with
our European allies.

00:13:28.407 --> 00:13:30.476
Say, guys, this
is your continent.

00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:32.444
You know, when this
thing comes in,

00:13:32.444 --> 00:13:33.679
let's bring this
in for a landing

00:13:33.679 --> 00:13:35.948
and then you guys
have to step up

00:13:35.948 --> 00:13:38.317
and meet your
security obligations.

00:13:38.317 --> 00:13:40.052
And part of what
animates that is,

00:13:40.052 --> 00:13:43.221
I think our primary
national security objective

00:13:43.221 --> 00:13:44.990
is to deter China.

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:46.324
And if we want to do that,

00:13:46.324 --> 00:13:48.427
we're gonna have
to do a lot more

00:13:48.427 --> 00:13:51.296
to project hard power
in the Indo-Pacific

00:13:51.296 --> 00:13:52.564
than we've been doing.

00:13:52.564 --> 00:13:56.001
I think Biden views the
top challenge as Europe.

00:13:56.001 --> 00:13:59.772
I think he views China as a
client, not as an adversary.

00:13:59.772 --> 00:14:01.106
I view China as an adversary

00:14:01.106 --> 00:14:04.376
and I think they're the
only ones in this world

00:14:04.376 --> 00:14:07.646
that could possibly compete
with us on a global scale.

00:14:09.014 --> 00:14:11.116
- What do you make of the
polling data right now?

00:14:11.116 --> 00:14:12.318
I know you don't
govern by polls.

00:14:12.318 --> 00:14:14.453
I've heard you
say it many times,

00:14:14.453 --> 00:14:16.054
but if we're to
believe the polls,

00:14:16.054 --> 00:14:18.257
you know, somehow Trump is at
50% or something like that.

00:14:18.257 --> 00:14:20.559
- Yeah, look, I
mean, I think that,

00:14:20.559 --> 00:14:22.861
you know, some of these primary
polls are what they are.

00:14:22.861 --> 00:14:25.864
I mean, you know, you
followed my reelection race,

00:14:25.864 --> 00:14:28.434
there were polls that had
me up by one or two points

00:14:28.434 --> 00:14:30.769
and I won by almost 20 points.

00:14:30.769 --> 00:14:34.773
And so sometimes when you
have this volume of polls,

00:14:34.773 --> 00:14:36.675
clearly polls are expensive.

00:14:36.675 --> 00:14:38.877
And so if you're
doing them every day,

00:14:38.877 --> 00:14:41.780
either someone's funding
that with an agenda or not.

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:42.915
But I also understand,

00:14:42.915 --> 00:14:45.784
you know, you're
running against somebody

00:14:45.784 --> 00:14:48.354
who is a hundred percent
name identification,

00:14:48.354 --> 00:14:50.689
probably the most famous person

00:14:50.689 --> 00:14:53.125
in the modern
history of politics.

00:14:53.125 --> 00:14:55.260
But what I think that it shows,

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:57.862
and I think we have data
after the debate to show this,

00:14:57.862 --> 00:14:59.731
is that, you know,
whatever he's at,

00:14:59.731 --> 00:15:01.867
he's got some that are
very hard for him for sure.

00:15:01.867 --> 00:15:03.902
And then he's got
a lot that are soft

00:15:03.902 --> 00:15:05.570
and those are people that,

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:09.140
you know, they're willing to
support somebody that's strong,

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:12.444
that has a record of delivering
on America First principles

00:15:12.444 --> 00:15:17.015
and that would be a big time
a change agent as president.

00:15:17.015 --> 00:15:18.884
They are not gonna
vote for somebody

00:15:18.884 --> 00:15:20.219
who's just gonna go back

00:15:20.219 --> 00:15:22.854
and be a managed
decline Republican.

00:15:22.854 --> 00:15:24.789
So if it's a choice
between Trump or that,

00:15:24.789 --> 00:15:26.291
they're gonna go Trump.

00:15:26.291 --> 00:15:28.394
But when they're presented
with my bio, my family,

00:15:28.394 --> 00:15:31.329
my accomplishments,
and our vision,

00:15:31.329 --> 00:15:32.898
you know, we do
convert those people.

00:15:32.898 --> 00:15:34.967
Now, we're having to
do this on the ground,

00:15:34.967 --> 00:15:38.636
going town to town in Iowa,
town to town in New Hampshire.

00:15:38.636 --> 00:15:41.907
And we've actually had a huge
amount of success in Iowa.

00:15:41.907 --> 00:15:43.142
I mean, if you look back

00:15:43.142 --> 00:15:45.210
at previous election cycles

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:48.814
and find where the Iowa caucus
winner was in the summer,

00:15:48.814 --> 00:15:51.550
people like Ted
Cruz and Santorum,

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.352
they were pulling
at like 5 or 6%.

00:15:53.352 --> 00:15:58.089
You know, we're clear second
in Iowa under any metric,

00:15:58.089 --> 00:15:59.858
everybody else is
in single digits.

00:15:59.858 --> 00:16:00.993
And so, I wouldn't trade places

00:16:00.993 --> 00:16:02.627
with anyone in Iowa right now.

00:16:02.627 --> 00:16:04.863
I think we're doing
what we need to do.

00:16:04.863 --> 00:16:08.600
And we are gonna outwork
everybody in those early states.

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:10.602
But once that starts to happen,

00:16:10.602 --> 00:16:12.871
that's what's gonna
make the big difference.

00:16:12.871 --> 00:16:14.039
So everything we're doing

00:16:14.039 --> 00:16:16.174
is geared towards
accumulating delegates.

00:16:16.174 --> 00:16:18.343
If we were trying to
juice national polls,

00:16:18.343 --> 00:16:21.213
then, you know, we would
try to advertise nationally

00:16:21.213 --> 00:16:22.680
and do some of those things.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:25.017
And so it's a state by state
thing, that's what we're doing.

00:16:25.017 --> 00:16:26.752
And we're happy with
the progress we've made,

00:16:26.752 --> 00:16:29.054
particularly over the last,
I think four to six weeks.

00:16:29.054 --> 00:16:31.323
I think we've solidified
a lot of support

00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:33.091
and we're building.

00:16:33.091 --> 00:16:35.226
- Do you want Trump to
show up to the next debate?

00:16:35.226 --> 00:16:36.862
I mean, the last one
was a little bizarre

00:16:36.862 --> 00:16:39.565
because you were clearly the
front runner at the debate

00:16:39.565 --> 00:16:41.166
and nobody was going after you

00:16:41.166 --> 00:16:44.303
and I bumped into you in
the hotel the next morning

00:16:44.303 --> 00:16:46.571
and you said, "Well, they
knew I was gonna hit back."

00:16:46.571 --> 00:16:48.741
And it seems like they
were sort of afraid,

00:16:48.741 --> 00:16:50.675
you know, Vivek, a
little bit, I suppose.

00:16:50.675 --> 00:16:53.011
But it seems like they
didn't wanna go after you.

00:16:53.011 --> 00:16:55.747
So the dynamics are
really bizarre right now.

00:16:55.747 --> 00:16:57.015
- Yeah, I mean, look,

00:16:57.015 --> 00:16:59.551
I think he owes it to
the public to debate.

00:16:59.551 --> 00:17:01.353
I think the idea
that he's entitled

00:17:01.353 --> 00:17:03.755
to be nominated is absurd.

00:17:03.755 --> 00:17:05.290
I think that there's
a lot of questions

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.691
that he needs to answer,

00:17:06.691 --> 00:17:09.495
both about how he
would win the election,

00:17:09.495 --> 00:17:11.330
but also about some
of the decisions

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.931
that he made as president.

00:17:12.931 --> 00:17:15.067
You pointed out the Fauci
and then there are others.

00:17:15.067 --> 00:17:16.801
So I think he should do it.

00:17:16.801 --> 00:17:19.371
He probably won't do
it, and that's fine.

00:17:19.371 --> 00:17:20.606
I'm gonna be there regardless.

00:17:20.606 --> 00:17:23.007
I do think you're gonna
see a smaller stage

00:17:23.007 --> 00:17:25.377
because I think some of those
folks aren't gonna qualify

00:17:25.377 --> 00:17:26.778
for this next round.

00:17:26.778 --> 00:17:28.713
And look, my thing is,

00:17:28.713 --> 00:17:30.915
you know, as far be it
for me to tell anyone

00:17:30.915 --> 00:17:32.317
who to run or not run,

00:17:32.317 --> 00:17:34.820
but you either have
a path or you don't.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.221
And if you don't have a path,

00:17:36.221 --> 00:17:38.122
then we should focus
on the candidates,

00:17:38.122 --> 00:17:41.326
you know, that have a
conceivable shot at this.

00:17:41.326 --> 00:17:43.462
I will say, though,
being on that stage,

00:17:43.462 --> 00:17:45.163
I think one of the reasons why

00:17:45.163 --> 00:17:49.034
I wasn't necessarily the target
as much as people thought is

00:17:49.034 --> 00:17:51.336
I have a record of success.

00:17:51.336 --> 00:17:53.839
I've done the things that
people are talking about

00:17:53.839 --> 00:17:55.707
that we need to do
for this country

00:17:55.707 --> 00:17:57.909
in Florida across the board.

00:17:57.909 --> 00:18:01.613
And so, I'm armed with the
ability to say that I've done it

00:18:01.613 --> 00:18:03.148
and also to point out,

00:18:03.148 --> 00:18:04.582
you know, whatever
shortcomings would be

00:18:04.582 --> 00:18:06.951
from somebody that's
lobbying a grenade my way.

00:18:06.951 --> 00:18:09.921
So I'm prepared to do
however it shakes out.

00:18:09.921 --> 00:18:11.990
But if it's just me
and I get something,

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:14.426
I wanna look into the camera
and tell people my vision

00:18:14.426 --> 00:18:16.728
of how to reverse this
country's decline,

00:18:16.728 --> 00:18:18.730
beat Biden and get
us on a better path.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:21.533
And I think we all know
we need to do that.

00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:23.468
I'm the one guy
that has a record

00:18:23.468 --> 00:18:25.036
of showing how it can be done

00:18:25.036 --> 00:18:26.939
with how we've
transformed Florida.

00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:28.673
- Let me ask you just two more.

00:18:28.673 --> 00:18:30.742
As you know, I'll have
you on this show anytime,

00:18:30.742 --> 00:18:33.479
but personally, I wanna
see you on the view.

00:18:33.479 --> 00:18:35.981
I wanna see you sit
down with those ladies,

00:18:35.981 --> 00:18:39.117
have them repeat that
hysterical nonsense.

00:18:39.117 --> 00:18:41.420
Anna, what's her name,
who lives in Florida

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:43.788
and says crazy things
about this state.

00:18:43.788 --> 00:18:46.725
Do you plan on going for those
fights a little bit more?

00:18:46.725 --> 00:18:48.259
'Cause to me, that's
where you shine

00:18:48.259 --> 00:18:51.096
and I think that that's what
people wanna see outta you.

00:18:51.096 --> 00:18:52.030
- Yeah, we might.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:53.031
I mean, I think we have done

00:18:53.031 --> 00:18:55.200
some of the more
corporate press,

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.136
you know, with like,
the NBC's and the CNN's.

00:18:58.136 --> 00:18:59.370
So you may see.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:00.638
I mean, look, I think,

00:19:00.638 --> 00:19:02.073
you know, The View,

00:19:02.073 --> 00:19:03.608
kind of the hysterical
stuff that they've put out,

00:19:03.608 --> 00:19:06.478
it can be a little
bit much at times.

00:19:06.478 --> 00:19:07.712
But who knows?

00:19:07.712 --> 00:19:09.181
You know, we may
end up doing that.

00:19:09.181 --> 00:19:10.115
But you know, I'm out and about

00:19:10.115 --> 00:19:11.383
when we do our campaign stuff,

00:19:11.383 --> 00:19:13.785
anyone can come and
ask us questions.

00:19:13.785 --> 00:19:15.287
We welcome that.

00:19:15.287 --> 00:19:17.455
You know, we've got the
typical corporate outlets

00:19:17.455 --> 00:19:19.424
that follow us around.

00:19:19.424 --> 00:19:22.961
- So my last question for
you is gonna be for my mom.

00:19:22.961 --> 00:19:25.563
My mom who is a
lifelong Democrat,

00:19:25.563 --> 00:19:29.000
but she has woke up to the
insanity of the Democrats.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.969
She knows how I
feel about Florida

00:19:30.969 --> 00:19:32.504
and that I've supported you,

00:19:32.504 --> 00:19:34.706
but the idea of voting
for a Republican

00:19:34.706 --> 00:19:37.442
still in her mind is tough.

00:19:37.442 --> 00:19:40.979
What would you say to that
person who's about to break?

00:19:40.979 --> 00:19:42.080
They've had it
with the Democrats,

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:44.016
they've had it with the woke,

00:19:44.016 --> 00:19:46.050
but the idea of really
making that move,

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:49.621
even though they part-time
live in Florida is a tough one.

00:19:49.621 --> 00:19:51.857
What's the sales
pitch right there?

00:19:51.857 --> 00:19:53.125
- Well, first I would just say

00:19:53.125 --> 00:19:54.359
I kind of understand that.

00:19:54.359 --> 00:19:56.661
You know, my grandmother
lived till she was 91

00:19:56.661 --> 00:19:58.729
in Western Pennsylvania.

00:19:58.729 --> 00:20:02.134
You know, her husband, my
grandfather was a steel worker

00:20:02.134 --> 00:20:04.669
and she never voted
for a Republican

00:20:04.669 --> 00:20:07.573
for any office in
her entire life.

00:20:07.573 --> 00:20:09.540
And basically,
she was, you know,

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:12.544
traditional Catholic,
had conservative views

00:20:12.544 --> 00:20:13.478
on a lot of things.

00:20:13.478 --> 00:20:14.746
But it was like she said,

00:20:14.746 --> 00:20:16.748
"Look, the Republicans
are only for the rich,

00:20:16.748 --> 00:20:18.650
the Democrats are for
the working people."

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:19.917
And I would just say that

00:20:19.917 --> 00:20:22.420
I think the parties
are really changing

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:23.655
in who they represent.

00:20:23.655 --> 00:20:24.922
I think the Democratic party,

00:20:24.922 --> 00:20:27.559
they're driven by
an elite ideology.

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:29.227
I mean, woke ideology,

00:20:29.227 --> 00:20:31.462
ultimately that's something
that came outta places

00:20:31.462 --> 00:20:34.700
like Berkeley and these
left wing institutions.

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:37.903
This is not like salt
of the earth ideology.

00:20:37.903 --> 00:20:41.173
These are elites trying to
cram this down your throat,

00:20:41.173 --> 00:20:43.775
trying to tell, you know,
your kindergartner daughter

00:20:43.775 --> 00:20:45.477
that she's actually a boy.

00:20:45.477 --> 00:20:48.614
That is not anything
that has ever sprung up

00:20:48.614 --> 00:20:50.716
from kind of the
salt of the earth.

00:20:50.716 --> 00:20:52.284
So I think what we're doing,

00:20:52.284 --> 00:20:55.120
at least me as a Republican,
what I conceive of my role

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:57.723
is to represent
common sense again,

00:20:57.723 --> 00:21:00.425
a restoration of
sanity in this country.

00:21:00.425 --> 00:21:02.160
And to do like what
we did in Florida,

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:04.362
you know, you can't
please everyone, Dave,

00:21:04.362 --> 00:21:08.533
but we took very strong
stands and we won 60-40.

00:21:08.533 --> 00:21:10.936
I can tell you 60% of the voters

00:21:10.936 --> 00:21:14.505
are not Republicans in Florida,
it's closer to like 36%.

00:21:14.505 --> 00:21:17.775
So we had to get independents
and some discerning Democrats

00:21:17.775 --> 00:21:21.046
to say, you know what, we
can't have an open border.

00:21:21.046 --> 00:21:22.380
We have to have security.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.316
We can't have crime
running the streets.

00:21:24.316 --> 00:21:26.050
We have to have the rule of law.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.720
We need an economy so
people can afford gas

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:31.890
and afford a home and
afford groceries again.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.259
We need these core
things of parents' rights

00:21:34.259 --> 00:21:37.195
to ensure parents are
involved with education.

00:21:37.195 --> 00:21:40.665
Those are things I think
that span party lines

00:21:40.665 --> 00:21:44.469
and that I think we can build
a strong movement behind.

00:21:44.469 --> 00:21:46.505
And it's really just
restoring the country

00:21:46.505 --> 00:21:48.974
to a sense of sanity.

00:21:48.974 --> 00:21:51.576
- All right, we're clipping
that and sending it to my mom.

00:21:51.576 --> 00:21:52.544
Thanks, gov.

00:21:52.544 --> 00:21:53.779
We'll see you on the trail.

